{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 62, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "והוא יושב בארץ הנגב", :translit "ve-hu yoshev be-eretz ha-negev", :gloss "and he dwelt in the land of the Negev"} {:he "ויצא יצחק לשוח בשדה", :translit "va-yetze yitzchak la-suach ba-sadeh", :gloss "and Isaac went out to meditate in the field"} {:he "הרוצה שיחכים ידרים", :translit "ha-rotzeh she-yachkim yadirim", :gloss "whoever wishes to become wise, let him face south"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition of adjacent verses: dwelling in the Negev (south) followed by Isaac's prayer, hinting at the south–wisdom association"}], :frame {:text "The Talmud states that one who wishes to become wise should face south, since the Table of the Temple Showbread was in the north and the Menorah was in the south (Bava Batra 25b). Isaac went out to meditate in the field (Genesis 24:63) immediately after the verse notes he dwelt in the land of the Negev — literally 'south.' The Ba'al HaTurim reads the juxtaposition as an allusion to this Talmudic teaching.", :sources ["Bava Batra 25b" "Genesis 24:62" "Genesis 24:63"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition of adjacent verses: dwelling in the Negev (south) followed by Isaac's prayer, hinting at the south–wisdom association", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:07:50.390742892Z", :model "glm-5.2"}